These tests are a variations on a simple "load an add function written
in Chapel and call it". It was written before Chapel's dynamic loading
feature supported loading Chapel libraries. As such, the programs all
attempted to load a Chapel library as a "foreign" C program and then
call into it, which *almost* worked.

However, because the Chapel library was not initialized, it crashed on
teardown instead of exiting gracefully.

Since Chapel now supports dynamically loading Chapel programs, I've
adjusted the tests to live in the new world. They all throw the flag
"--no-builtin-runtime" in order to gracefully load the Chapel runtime
as a dynamic library.

Additionally, the 'exit(0)' calls have been removed, as the Chapel
runtime now cleans itself up properly (because all programs are using
the same copy).
